SCENARIO:
ACS Consulting, a small defense contractor, has inherited a
poorly configured network. The firewall allows all traffic,
has no segmentation, no logging, and dangerous services are
exposed to the internet. You must fix EVERYTHING.

PROBLEMS TO FIX:
  1. Allow Any Any on LAN (no deny-by-default)
  2. WAN allows all inbound traffic
  3. Telnet exposed to internet (port 23)
  4. No VLANs (flat network)
  5. No logging enabled
  6. No NAT rules for proper service publishing

YOUR TASKS:

TASK 1: IMPLEMENT DENY-BY-DEFAULT
  [ ] Remove all "Allow Any" rules
  [ ] Create specific allow rules for required services
  [ ] Add default deny as last rule

TASK 2: SECURE THE WAN
  [ ] Block all inbound WAN traffic by default
  [ ] Remove Telnet exposure
  [ ] Only allow necessary inbound services (if any)

TASK 3: CREATE NETWORK SEGMENTATION
  [ ] Create at least 2 VLANs (e.g., Servers, Workstations)
  [ ] Configure inter-VLAN rules
  [ ] Isolate sensitive resources

TASK 4: ENABLE LOGGING
  [ ] Enable logging on block rules
  [ ] Enable logging on key allow rules
  [ ] Verify logs appear in Status > System Logs

TASK 5: VERIFY COMMUNICATIONS
  [ ] DNS works (to DC01)
  [ ] Web browsing works
  [ ] Internal services accessible
  [ ] External attacks blocked

TASK 6: PRODUCE ASSESSMENT EVIDENCE
  [ ] Screenshot of final firewall rules
  [ ] Screenshot of VLAN configuration
  [ ] Screenshot of firewall logs
  [ ] Completed compliance checklist
  [ ] Network diagram with boundaries marked

GRADING:
  This lab is the practical assessment for the SC module.
  All 6 tasks must be completed with evidence.

